 behavior in the chicken embryo.</article-title><source>Dev Biol.</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>533</fpage><lpage>745</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13952299</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002971-Ho1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Donovan</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Regionalization and intersegmental coordination of rhythm-generating networks in the spinal cord of the chicken embryo.</article-title><source>J Neurosci.</source><volume>13(4)</volume><fpage>1354</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8463824</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002971-Chub1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chub</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Donovan</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Blockade and recovery of spontaneous rhythmic activity after application of neurotransmitter antagonists to spinal networks of the chicken embryo.</article-title><source>J Neurosci.</source><volume>18(1)</volume><fpage>294</fpage><lpage>306</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9412508</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002971-Usiak1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Usiak</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Landmesser</surname><given-names>LT</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Neuromuscular activity blockade induced by muscimol and d-tubocurarine differentially affects the survival of embryonic chicken motoneurons.</article-title><source>J Neurosci.</source><volume>19(18)</volume><fpage>7925</fpage><lpage>39</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10479694</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pon